      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "summary": "What this topic covers.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "topic-map",
          "html": "<p>Surveillance is watching people at scale &mdash; by governments, police, employers or companies. It includes cameras and facial recognition, licence-plate readers, phone location tracking, and the mass collection of internet traffic. Knowing what is being collected, and where, helps you decide when to take extra care &mdash; for example at a protest or crossing a border.</p>"
        }
